  "interpretation": [
    "The source-context arm produced a large, repeated primary recall increase: +31/48 route-item detections in Run 1 and +35/48 in Run 2. All four routes had strictly positive deltas in both runs.",
    "Aggregate runtime-control candidate counts decreased from A to B (10 to 6 in Run 1; 11 to 3 in Run 2), so added source did not create a general increase in candidate volume.",
    "The registered adoption decision nevertheless fails. In Run 1, Codex produced two new objective B-arm control candidates (P010 and P016), exceeding the per-route maximum of one.",
    "Post-run source adjudication also confirmed one frozen control contamination: P005 says spread requires same-faction membership, while the code accepts any target with positive reaction. The preregistered zero-contamination gate therefore fails both runs and forbids adopting B as the default.",
    "The appropriate conclusion is evidence that bounded Lua context materially improves detection on this finite mutant benchmark, not approval of the current B protocol for later phases. No item was replaced, repaired or rescored after outcomes, and no third run was made."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The estimand is limited to this frozen 12-item runtime-mutant benchmark.",
    "Surface items are negative controls and runtime controls are guardrails, not additional primary recall units.",
    "Route and run observations are repeated measurements, not independent draws from a defined model superpopulation.",
    "The pre-inference CLEAN audit missed P005's friendly-reaction versus same-faction distinction; this demonstrates that clean-control verification, not only reviewer behavior, limits the current experiment.",
    "Codex required two pre-inference response-format compatibility attempts, and GLM envelopes required reversible parser normalization. Both are preserved and excluded from model scoring as documented in HARNESS-AMENDMENT.json."
  ],
  "next_step": "Do not treat this as a third-run invitation. If source context is tested again, create runtime-source-context-pilot-v2 with a newly frozen control audit that checks faction/reaction semantics, positional format metadata and direct-callee coverage before any model call; later phases should inherit context_policy=A unless separately frozen otherwise."
